# Ignore all uasset and umap files in the root Content directory by default
# This is to prevent accidental check-in of test maps or assets not in proper folders.
# Specific subfolders under Content should be explicitly un-ignored if needed.
# Example: !Content/MySpecificFolder/
# /Content/*.uasset
# /Content/*.umap

# If you use LFS, you might want to track large asset files.
# Example:
# *.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# *.umap filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# For this project, we will assume no LFS initially.
# If project grows, LFS for .uasset and .umap under /Content/Art and /Content/Blueprints might be needed.
# For now, keep them versioned.
# !Content/Art/**/*.uasset
# !Content/Art/**/*.umap
# !Content/Blueprints/**/*.uasset
# !Content/Blueprints/**/*.umap

# However, for a clean start, it's better to not ignore them by default and let the user
# manage what they put into the Content folder directly.
# The structure provided in Design.md implies that assets will be in subfolders.
# So, let's not ignore .uasset and .umap in /Content/ for now.

